    "body": "## Summary\n- validate authenticated persisted actor identity before all user-scoped payout eligibility, history, request, and cancellation paths\n- prevent payout, verification, wallet, provider, and user persistence access for missing/transient principals\n- add regression coverage asserting zero financial-state interactions before the guard\n- document the payout-specific security invariant\n\n## Risk addressed\nPayout operations handle private financial state and money movement. Some paths previously dereferenced or queried with `currentUser.getId()` before a shared fail-closed identity guard, leaving service-level behavior dependent on upstream HTTP authentication and allowing transient/missing principals to reach financial state code paths.\n\n## Validation\nGitHub Actions must pass on the exact PR head before merge. Merge is permitted only via merge commit after re-checking master and exact-head checks.",
